{
  "id": "rop",
  "term": "ROP",
  "definition": "ROP refers to retinopathy of prematurity, a condition seen in preterm infants that is closely linked with prematurity, low birth weight, neonatal illness severity, oxygen exposure, and other perinatal risks. In developmental research, it is viewed not only as an eye disorder but also as a possible clinical marker of broader neurodevelopmental vulnerability, including later cognitive, motor, and behavioral difficulties.",
